#567 fbctrlcmdkill -- PRE-TABLE ADDENDUM for kill table 3a, written 2026-10-19 BEFORE the table runs (this file's mtime is
the order proof).  INSTRUMENT: probe v2 (99 rows, killtable2_20261019/probe.v2.frozen.py.txt).  BASELINE: the fix, in
/tmp/gx567.  Table 3a measures, on v2, the cells the F2 adjudication pass raised (GPT-6 Astra, f2/codex_fbcmdf2.txt) and
the grid they belong to.

THE CLASS, AND WHY IT IS CLOSED WHOLE.  Pass 2 found the width axis open on the accept side (E13: every accepted COMMAND
write was `sw'); F2 found it open again one cell over -- the only accepted `sd' command is a NOP, whose dispatch nothing
can observe, so a bound or a dispatch conditioned on `len == 8' passes.  Two consecutive passes, one class: the carrier's
class-closure amendment owes the WHOLE width x bound-edge grid in one diff.  The compare's generating set is its regions,
pinned at its edges (rule D2): ACCEPT 2 (any downward bound move refuses 2 first) and REFUSE 3 (any upward move accepts 3
first), at each width the producer emits -- sb, sh, sw, sd.  On v2:
    accept 2 (a GET, whose dispatch zeroes X1):  sb A:get   sh --   sw L, seeds   sd --
    refuse 3:                                    sb R:sb3   sh --   sw R:3        sd --
Plus the latch's persistence across intervening traffic (F2 question 4): no session refuses, accepts or reads, and
refuses again.

